Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 20:36:30 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 10817/11171] The .605 test closed both the planner defect and
 my regression

Milestone .605 planned at 00:25Z with the corrected instruction loaded, the
conductor having re-exec'd at 21:50Z against a fix committed at 21:13Z. Verified
id-for-id rather than from the summary line: the YAML holds 12 tasks exp6911 through
exp6922, the document declares "12 tasks, exp6911 through exp6922, in the exact
order listed below", the id lists are equal, and every declared id appears in the
document body.

That closes both failures in one run. The original defect was a document
over-claiming tasks the YAML never held -- .602 claimed 11 against 4, .603 claimed 13
against 4. My regression was the planner skipping the document altogether, which
.604 exhibited by running under a .603 document.

The test was filed in advance with both branches stated: rewritten and matching
closes it, skipped again means my instruction was not the cause. It was rewritten and
it matches, so the instruction was load-bearing and the both-files-required wording
stays. The "write FILE 2 first" ordering that caused the regression stays deleted.

Recorded but not claimed: .605 planned 12 tasks against .604's 7 and .603's 4. Task
count varies for reasons this did not measure, and a later reader should not read the
recovery as an effect of this change.

Still open: .604 continues against its stale .603 document. A prompt fix reaches
future planning runs and cannot repair an already-activated milestone.

